.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Von Laue (1912) predicted that a crystal, as a periodic array of scatterers, should diffract X-rays like a grating, and Friedrich and Knipping saw the discrete spots. Summing the waves from N periodically spaced scatterers with structure_factor gives the Laue interference function: intensity N^2 at integer h (the Laue condition) and almost nothing in between, ever sharper as N grows.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/crystal/xrd/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_02_laue_interference_thumb.png
